    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "A Judgment on Babylon"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A pronouncement concerning the desert by the sea:",
          "Like storms that pass over the Negev,",
          "it comes from the desert, from the land of terror."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A troubling vision is declared to me:",
          "“The treacherous one acts treacherously,",
          "and the destroyer destroys.",
          "Advance, Elam! Lay siege, you Medes!",
          "I will put an end to all the groaning.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Therefore I am filled with anguish.",
          "Pain grips me, like the pain of a woman in labor.",
          "I am too perplexed to hear,",
          "too dismayed to see."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "My heart staggers;",
          "horror terrifies me.",
          "He has turned my last glimmer of hope",
          "into sheer terror."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Prepare a table, and spread out a carpet!",
          "Eat and drink!",
          "Rise up, you princes, and oil the shields!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For the Lord has said to me,",
          "“Go, post a lookout;",
          "let him report what he sees."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "When he sees riders —",
          "pairs of horsemen,",
          "riders on donkeys,",
          "riders on camels —",
          "he must pay close attention.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then the lookout reported,",
          "“Lord, I stand on the watchtower all day,",
          "and I stay at my post all night."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Look, riders come —",
          "horsemen in pairs.”",
          "And he answered, saying,",
          "“Babylon has fallen, has fallen.",
          "All the images of her gods",
          "have been shattered on the ground.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "My people who have been crushed",
          "on the threshing floor,",
          "I have declared to you",
          "what I have heard from the Lord of Armies,",
          "the God of Israel."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "A Pronouncement against Dumah"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A pronouncement concerning Dumah: ,",
          "One calls to me from Seir,",
          "“Watchman, what is left of the night?",
          "Watchman, what is left of the night? ”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The watchman said,",
          "“Morning has come, and also night.",
          "If you want to ask, ask!",
          "Come back again.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "A Pronouncement against Arabia"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A pronouncement concerning Arabia:",
          "In the desert brush",
          "you will camp for the night,",
          "you caravans of Dedanites."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Bring water for the thirsty.",
          "The inhabitants of the land of Tema",
          "meet the refugees with food."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For they have fled from swords,",
          "from the drawn sword,",
          "from the bow that is strung,",
          "and from the stress of battle."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For the Lord said this to me: “Within one year, as a hired worker counts years, all the glory of Kedar will be gone."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The remaining Kedarite archers will be few in number.” For the Lord, the God of Israel, has spoken."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
